# Citation metadata for Synapse (Citation File Format 1.2.0,
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub shows it as
# "Cite this repository". When the project is published, add
# "repository-code", "license" and "date-released" (see
# docs/RELEASE_NOTES.md, "Before the first release").
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Synapse in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Synapse: a transparent, sequence-centric DNA analysis workbench"
abstract: >-
  Synapse is a terminal and Python workbench for DNA, RNA and protein
  sequence analysis: sequence statistics, open reading frames under all
  27 NCBI genetic codes, RNA and protein properties, restriction digests
  and cloning, primer design, mutation and variant analysis with HGVS
  notation, BLAST and literature search. Every result records its method,
  parameters and limitations. The calculations are compared with
  established tools and curated data (Primer3, NCBI ORFfinder, bcftools,
  Mutalyzer, ExPASy ProtParam, ViennaRNA, the RefSeq annotation of
  Escherichia coli K-12 and ClinVar). Synapse is research and teaching
  software and is not experimentally or clinically validated.
authors:
  - given-names: Onur
    family-names: Bayraktar
version: 0.2.0.dev0
url: "https://synapse-gen.com"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence analysis
  - open reading frame
  - primer design
  - restriction analysis
  - HGVS
  - BLAST
